# BuildKit build-context exclusions.
#
# The CI pipeline runs lint + test BEFORE build and populates the Go module
# + build caches INSIDE the repo directory (per .gitlab-ci.yml — GOMODCACHE
# and GOCACHE are pinned to ${CI_PROJECT_DIR}/.go/{mod,build}). By the time
# the build stage hands the context to BuildKit, `.go/` typically holds
# 3 GiB+ of cached modules and compiled object files — none of which the
# Dockerfile needs (the builder stage runs its own `go mod download` from
# Athens). Sending it anyway pushes 8+ minutes onto every pipeline.
#
# Likewise, security/test artifacts that earlier stages emit and pass via
# `needs: artifacts: true` end up in CI_PROJECT_DIR before build runs and
# don't belong in the image.
#
# Diagnosed 2026-06-04 when a routine falcon-id rebuild took 30+ minutes;
# BuildKit log showed `#5 transferring context: 3.30GB 502.1s`. With this
# .dockerignore the same context drops to <100 MB and BuildKit context
# upload completes in <30 seconds.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets — keep dev .env files out of the image
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.secret

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Git — the COPY happens against a tar of the working tree, so .git
# adds 40+ MB of pack history that the builder never reads.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Go caches — THIS is the 3 GiB the CI used to upload every build.
# Pinned to ${CI_PROJECT_DIR}/.go/{mod,build} by .gitlab-ci.yml so the
# lint/test stages can reuse modules without re-downloading; the build
# stage's BuildKit context doesn't need any of it because the Dockerfile
# does its own `go mod download`.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.go/
**/.go/

# Local-developer caches in case anyone runs `go build` outside CI
# and ends up with a bin/ checked in.
bin/
dist/
build/
*.test
*.exe
*.out
coverage.out
coverage.html
cover.out

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test fixtures + test files — the Dockerfile builds only main packages,
# but BuildKit transfers everything in the context tar anyway. Excluding
# *_test.go files alone saves a few MB; excluding testdata/ saves more.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*_test.go
**/testdata
**/testdata/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CI artifacts from earlier stages that arrive via `needs: artifacts: true`
# and otherwise hitch a ride into the build context.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gosec-report.json
sbom.json
sbom*.json
sbom*.xml
harbor-trivy-*.json
trivy-*.json

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IDE / editor + local tool detritus
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# K6 load-test scripts + non-Go docs.
#
# IMPORTANT: do NOT exclude `docs/` wholesale — `docs/docs.go` is the
# swag-generated Swagger spec that `cmd/routes.go` imports as
# `github.com/dogukanturhal/falcon-id/docs`. Excluding it breaks the
# build with "no required module provides package".
# Exclude markdown / non-Go subdirs explicitly instead.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
k6/
docs/*.md
docs/audits/
docs/compliance/
docs/integrations/
docs/operator-runbooks/
hack/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Helm chart values + deployment manifests — written by CI's
# bump-manifest stage AFTER build; never inputs to the image.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
deploy/
